From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:05:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/59] fix(pbs): show PBS's reason when it refuses the backup
 session

Any refusal of the backup/reader protocol upgrade was reported as
"PBS authentication failed: HTTP ...", with the raw response headers
appended. PBS also refuses with 400 ("backup owner check failed"),
403 (missing privilege) or 404 ("namespace not found"), so users went
looking for a password problem.

The error now carries the status code and the response body only, and
its wording follows the status:
- 401: PBS authentication failed (HTTP 401): <reason>
- 403: PBS access denied (HTTP 403): <reason>
- other: PBS refused the backup (HTTP <code>): <reason>
The reason is the body (or its JSON "message"), whitespace-collapsed,
falling back to the status text when empty. Headers stay in the debug
log. The AuthErr type is kept.
